; Silence bootc's expected mac_admin probe in ordinary services (#1198).
;
; `bootc status` probes for mac_admin by running chcon with a label the policy
; does not define (bootc lsm.rs, selinux_ensure_install). Outside install_t
; the probe is denied, bootc re-executes itself once and probes again, then
; carries on: the denial is the answer it expects. Run from a plain service
; (common's projectbluefin-countme, any script that calls bootc) it logs two
;
;   avc: denied { mac_admin } capability=33
;        scontext=system_u:system_r:unconfined_service_t:s0 tclass=capability2
;
; on every boot. dontaudit, not allow: granting mac_admin would let every
; unconfined service write labels the policy does not know, and would change
; what bootc's probe decides. A capability check has no target but the
; process itself, so this domain plus one permission is the narrowest rule
; the policy language can express. Installed at build time (the store is on
; read-only /usr once booted, #551); the desktop contract's [selinux] modules
; list asserts it is loaded.
(dontaudit unconfined_service_t self (capability2 (mac_admin)))
